  "worked_solution": "To find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{2y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
